WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.222
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online TOEIC preparation.

2
00:00:05.522 --> 00:00:08.909
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.209 --> 00:00:16.343
Unit twenty: TOEIC Test Strategy and Timing. Today you will plan your timing, guessing and review across all seven parts.

4
00:00:16.643 --> 00:00:19.260
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:23.502
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:25.154
Timing.

7
00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:28.161
Timing means how you divide your time.

8
00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:30.552
Good timing helps your score.

9
00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:33.640
Your turn. Say: Timing.

10
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:37.339
Timing.

11
00:00:38.083 --> 00:00:38.852
Pace.

12
00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:41.768
Pace means the speed you work at.

13
00:00:42.383 --> 00:00:43.872
Keep a steady pace.

14
00:00:44.483 --> 00:00:46.799
Your turn. Say: Pace.

15
00:00:49.633 --> 00:00:50.507
Pace.

16
00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:52.158
Guess.

17
00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:55.428
Guess means to choose without being sure.

18
00:00:56.017 --> 00:00:57.354
Guess if you do not know.

19
00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:00.335
Your turn. Say: Guess.

20
00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:04.050
Guess.

21
00:01:04.817 --> 00:01:05.899
Eliminate.

22
00:01:06.883 --> 00:01:09.405
Eliminate means to remove wrong options.

23
00:01:10.017 --> 00:01:12.039
Eliminate two options first.

24
00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:15.395
Your turn. Say: Eliminate.

25
00:01:18.233 --> 00:01:19.362
Eliminate.

26
00:01:20.117 --> 00:01:20.793
Skip.

27
00:01:21.783 --> 00:01:24.131
Skip means to leave a question for later.

28
00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:26.321
Skip a long question.

29
00:01:26.917 --> 00:01:29.023
Your turn. Say: Skip.

30
00:01:31.867 --> 00:01:32.566
Skip.

31
00:01:33.317 --> 00:01:34.318
Answer sheet.

32
00:01:35.317 --> 00:01:38.129
Answer sheet means the paper where you mark answers.

33
00:01:38.717 --> 00:01:40.716
Mark the answer sheet carefully.

34
00:01:41.317 --> 00:01:43.981
Your turn. Say: Answer sheet.

35
00:01:46.833 --> 00:01:47.881
Answer sheet.

36
00:01:48.617 --> 00:01:49.699
Consistent.

37
00:01:50.683 --> 00:01:53.647
Consistent means regular and the same each time.

38
00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:56.099
Be consistent in practice.

39
00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:59.788
Your turn. Say: Consistent.

40
00:02:02.633 --> 00:02:03.600
Consistent.

41
00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:05.456
Weak point.

42
00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:09.297
Weak point means an area where you need improvement.

43
00:02:09.883 --> 00:02:11.244
Find your weak point.

44
00:02:11.850 --> 00:02:14.375
Your turn. Say: Weak point.

45
00:02:17.233 --> 00:02:18.118
Weak point.

46
00:02:18.933 --> 00:02:22.758
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:23.617 --> 00:02:26.719
Visal, how should I use time in the Reading section?

48
00:02:27.817 --> 00:02:39.954
You have seventy-five minutes for one hundred questions. Spend about twenty-five minutes on Parts 5 and 6, so that you have fifty minutes for Part 7.

49
00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:42.399
What about guessing?

50
00:02:43.483 --> 00:02:52.649
There is no penalty for wrong answers, so never leave a blank. Eliminate options you know are wrong, then guess from those that remain.

51
00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:55.227
How should I practise?

52
00:02:56.317 --> 00:03:06.341
Take timed practice tests, find your weak points and repeat them. Be consistent: thirty minutes every day is better than five hours once a month.

53
00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:09.058
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:09.917 --> 00:03:14.215
Grammar focus: Strategy: time plan, no blanks, weak points.

55
00:03:14.515 --> 00:03:15.771
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:16.483 --> 00:03:20.561
I spend about twenty-five minutes on Parts 5 and 6.

57
00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:24.042
There is no penalty, so I never leave a blank.

58
00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:30.831
Follow a time plan, answer every question, and practise your weak points regularly with timed tests.

59
00:03:31.583 --> 00:03:35.269
Be careful! Don't say: I leave hard questions blank.

60
00:03:37.233 --> 00:03:39.535
Say: I guess; there is no penalty.

61
00:03:39.835 --> 00:03:41.265
Never leave blanks.

62
00:03:42.067 --> 00:03:45.253
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:46.067 --> 00:03:47.462
A Practice Plan.

64
00:03:47.762 --> 00:03:50.911
Mealea takes a full practice test every Sunday.

65
00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:54.364
She notes which parts take too much time.

66
00:03:55.367 --> 00:03:57.982
She discovers that Part 7 is her weak point.

67
00:03:58.967 --> 00:04:02.510
Every day she reads one email and one notice for thirty minutes.

68
00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:06.126
After two months her timing and score improve.

69
00:04:07.233 --> 00:04:11.014
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:13.490
How many minutes for Reading?

71
00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:17.757
A, forty-five. B, ten. C, seventy-five.

72
00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:23.520
The answer is C: seventy-five.

73
00:04:24.683 --> 00:04:26.938
Is there a penalty for wrong answers?

74
00:04:27.238 --> 00:04:30.834
A, no. B, yes. C, only in Part 1.

75
00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:36.272
The answer is A: no.

76
00:04:37.417 --> 00:04:39.254
Mealea's weak point is blank.

77
00:04:39.554 --> 00:04:43.416
A, Part 2. B, Part 7. C, Part 1.

78
00:04:46.967 --> 00:04:49.129
The answer is B: Part 7.

79
00:04:50.283 --> 00:04:51.644
Practice should be blank.

80
00:04:51.944 --> 00:04:55.992
A, rare. B, only before the test. C, consistent.

81
00:04:59.533 --> 00:05:01.719
The answer is C: consistent.

82
00:05:02.883 --> 00:05:05.626
About how long on Parts 5 and 6?

83
00:05:05.926 --> 00:05:10.868
A, twenty-five minutes. B, five minutes. C, sixty minutes.

84
00:05:14.433 --> 00:05:17.594
The answer is A: twenty-five minutes.

85
00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:22.068
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:22.917 --> 00:05:25.148
What is your plan for TOEIC test day?

87
00:05:33.950 --> 00:05:35.497
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:35.797 --> 00:05:50.735
I will follow a time plan: about twenty-five minutes for Parts 5 and 6 and the rest for Part 7. I will answer every question because there is no penalty. Before the test I will practise my weak points every day.

89
00:05:51.035 --> 00:05:52.605
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:53.517 --> 00:05:59.617
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: time plan, no blanks, weak points.

91
00:05:59.917 --> 00:06:05.275
Today's value is self-discipline. Control your habits, so your habits do not control you.

92
00:06:05.575 --> 00:06:11.678
Congratulations! You have finished Online TOEIC preparation. See you in Online Cambridge exams!

93
00:06:11.978 --> 00:06:14.688
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

